{
  "Recurring appointments based on RFC 5545 rules, with exceptions and individually edited occurrences, a prompt that asks what a change should apply to, a recurrence editor, and time zone support that handles daylight saving time.": "",
  "Recurring appointments": "Yinelenen randevular",
  "An appointment with a `recurrenceRule` is a series, and the scheduler shows its occurrences only in the visible days. `recurrenceException` excludes specific times, and an appointment whose `recurrenceId` references a series replaces one of its occurrences. Supported parts are `FREQ` (daily to yearly), `INTERVAL`, `COUNT`, `UNTIL`, `BYDAY` (`2MO`, `-1FR`), `BYMONTHDAY`, `BYMONTH`, `BYYEARDAY`, `BYWEEKNO`, `BYSETPOS`, `WKST`, `BYHOUR` and `BYMINUTE`.": "",
  "Editing a series": "",
  "Moving, resizing, the form and Delete all ask the same question. **This one**: a new appointment takes its place, referencing its series, and its time is excluded from the series. **This and following**: the series ends before it (with `UNTIL` or a smaller `COUNT`), and a new series continues from it. **The whole series**: every occurrence moves the same way, and moving a weekly series to another day moves its weekdays.": "",
  "With a data source, each write goes through its adapter in sequence: new rows first, then updates, then deletes. If a later write fails, the earlier ones are rolled back through the adapter. `onDataError` reports what was saved (`saved`, `unsaved`) and whether everything was rolled back (`undone`). An individually edited occurrence is an ordinary row linked to its series through `recurrenceId`, and deleting the series requests those rows from the adapter, whether they are loaded or not. This example uses a data source.": "",
  "Recurrence editor": "",
  "The appointment form includes it (`editing.allowRecurrence`). On its own, it is `RecurrenceEditor`, with the repeat list, the interval, the weekdays, a day of the month or a weekday by position, the month and the end. A rule it cannot fully display stays unchanged until a selection is changed.": "",
  "Time zones": "Saat dilimleri",
  "`timeZone` displays days and hours in a given zone. A series recurs in the zone of its start (`startDateTimeZone`), so 09:00 in New York stays 09:00 there across daylight saving changes. On the night the clocks go forward, the skipped hour is passed, and a time inside it moves forward by the hour. On the night they go back, an appointment's box is as long as the appointment lasts.": "",
  "With `editing.allowTimeZones`, the form has a time zone picker and a **Separate end time zone** check box. When checked, a second picker sets the end zone, and an appointment with a different end zone opens with it checked. When unchecked, the end follows the start zone again.": "",
  "Chooses this occurrence, this and following, or the whole series.": "",
  "Confirms, or cancels so that the change is discarded and the appointment reverts.": "",
  "An occurrence is named with how its series repeats, and an individually edited one says so. The indicators are decorative (`aria-hidden`).": "",
  "A modal form with radio buttons under the question. The first option is selected.": "",
  "A group named \"Repeat\". The weekdays are toggle buttons (`aria-pressed`) in a group named by its label, and the description is polite live text.": "",
  "Units: the indicators (`bar`, `chip`, `open`, `past`, `disabled`). A design language without them omits them.": "",
  "Unit: the tooltip line that describes the recurrence (`exception`).": "",
  "The editor, its weekday buttons and its description.": "",
  "Units of the editor. `day-button` is the place for the weekday buttons, plus `row-gap` and `column-gap`.": "",
  "`null` uses the browser time zone": "",
  "The time zone for days and hours, as an IANA name (`Europe/Istanbul`). Conversion uses `Intl` only.": "",
  "What changing or deleting an occurrence applies to. `ask` prompts the user. In code, it applies to the occurrence unless the call specifies otherwise.": "",
  "The indicators of an occurrence and of an individually edited one, where the design language draws them.": "",
  "Includes the recurrence editor in the form.": "",
  "Includes a time zone picker and a \"Separate end time zone\" check box in the form (`separateEndZone` in the form `data` and `items`), which shows a picker for the end. When unchecked, the end follows the start zone. It is not available for all-day appointments.": "",
  "The recurrence, as an RFC 5545 rule (`FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=MO,WE`). Leave it empty for a single appointment.": "",
  "The excluded times (`EXDATE`), as comma-separated text (`20261104T090000Z,…`) or a list of dates.": "",
  "On an individually edited occurrence, the key of its series.": "",
  "The time zones of the start (and the series) and the end. Leave them empty to use the scheduler zone for the start and the start zone for the end.": "",
  "For an occurrence, `scope` sets what the change applies to: `occurrence`, `following` or `series`.": "",
  "The same for a delete.": "Silme için aynısı.",
  "Asks the user what a change (`update`) or a delete (`delete`) applies to. Resolves to the answer, or `null`.": "",
  "The series of an occurrence or an individually edited one, the series itself, or otherwise `null`.": "",
  "Indicate an occurrence generated from a rule, and an occurrence edited individually from its series.": "",
  "The occurrences of a series in a time range.": "",
  "Describes the recurrence in plain words in the current locale.": "",
  "`{ appointment, series, action, scopes, scope, cancel }`. Set `scope` to answer without prompting, narrow `scopes`, or cancel the change.": "",
  "`{ appointment, series, action, scope, byUser }`. `scope` is `null` when the prompt was canceled.": "",
  "These also include `scope` and `series` (`null` for a non-recurring appointment). `Updated` includes `added`, which is the individually edited occurrence or the continuing series.": "",
  "These also include `scope` and `series`.": "",
  "This also includes `saved` and `unsaved` (each `{ kind, appointment, changes? }`) and `undone`, which report what a series change wrote before failing and whether it was rolled back.": "",
  "RecurrenceEditor": "RecurrenceEditor",
  "The rule as RFC 5545 text, empty when it does not repeat. `x-model` provides two-way binding.": "",
  "Now": "",
  "The start of the series. A rule takes its weekday and day of the month from it, unless the rule specifies them.": "",
  "Writes the last date as a date, instead of the end of that day in UTC.": "",
  "The browser time zone": "",
  "The time zone the series recurs in.": "",
  "The options in the repeat list.": "",
  "The first weekday button, names and strings, read-only state, and the description line.": "",
  "The rule parsed from `value`, and its description in words. Reactive.": "",
  "Occurs when a selection changes the rule.": "",
  "Utilities": "",
  "A time zone: `wall(moment)`, `moment(wall, later?)`, `offset`, `dayStart`, `addDays`, `sameDay`, `toLocal` and `fromLocal` (for editors), and `TimeZone.names()`.": "",
  "Converts a rule to an object (`RecurrenceRule`) and back.": "",
  "The times a rule occurs in a range, as wall clock times.": "",
  "Describes a rule in plain words.": "",
  "Exception dates as stored in the field.": "",
  "The data layer filter for a range: it starts before the range ends and either ends at or after the range starts or has a rule. The scheduler's `remoteFiltering` uses it.": ""
